  "summary": "New preprints extend ensemble generation to complexes and RNA, while benchmarks expose cofolding limits and ligand strain gets neural-potential estimates.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is moving from single static structures to conformational ensembles and transition pathways. OriDynamics targets all-atom ensembles for monomers and complexes, REVEAL chains secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2, unbiased MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR RNA, and the CYFIP1-eIF4E study combines funnel-restrained TAMD on Martini 3 with beta-VAE clustering to resolve three recurring binding modes. A transition-conditioned fingerprint ranks players within rare-event corridors. Published work adds grounding: a cofolding benchmark of AlphaFold3, RoseTTAFold3, Boltz-2 and Chai-1 finds ligand placement decoupled from protein conformation accuracy, and AIMNet2-CPCM estimates ligand strain across ~8K PDB ligands. New here is pairing generative ensemble methods with explicit evaluation of conformational accuracy and bound-state energetics.",
